    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "The Global Land Ice Measurements from Space (GLIMS) Glacier Database is a multi-temporal geospatial database of glacier outlines, debris covered regions of glaciers, supraglacial and proglacial lakes, seasonal snowlines, and glacier centerlines.\u00a0The database contains at least one outline for all of the Earth\u2019s 274,000 glaciers.\u00a0Glacier outlines are mapped by a global collective of glaciologists from academic institutions and national and state agencies.\u00a0The majority of glacier outlines are derived from optical satellite and aerial imagery.\u00a0The earliest outlines, from 1450, are created by mapping moraines.\u00a0The database also includes outlines for the late 19th century that have been mapped from paper maps, mostly in the European Alps.\u00a0Most outlines are mapped by hand.\u00a0Automated or semi-automated mapping methods are also employed but are also edited by hand to ensure data quality.\u00a0New glacier data are periodically added to the database.",
